  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vale-cli/vale/tarball/v3.24.0",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vale-cli/vale/zipball/v3.24.0",
  "body": "This release adds `vale test`, a test runner for your rules. A rule that matches nothing still loads, runs, and reports success. You only find out it's broken when it misses something. Now each rule can carry its own test cases: a short document, and the alerts linting it should produce.\r\n\r\n    extends: existence\r\n    message: \"Consider removing '%s'.\"\r\n    tokens:\r\n      - perhaps\r\n    tests:\r\n      - name: flags a hedge\r\n        input: Perhaps we should ship.\r\n        want: |\r\n          1:1:House.Hedging:Consider removing 'Perhaps'.\r\n\r\nRunning `vale test` lints each case and shows a diff when the output doesn't match. A case can pin the exact output (`want`), check for part of it (`contains`), or check that something is left alone (`absent`). It can run one rule on its own or go through your project's configuration, and it can read its input as another format or through a View. `script` rules are tested the same way. `--coverage` fails any rule that no case makes fire, and the exit codes are built for CI.\r\n\r\nSee [Testing](https://docs.vale.sh/topics/testing) and the [announcement post](https://vale.sh/blog/testing-rules).\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 2ee78171 fix: A rule whose `tests` don't parse fails `vale test` instead of vanishing\r\n* 77da0b08 refactor: Typed errors, pattern errors at the token, and readable contexts\r\n* 634b321c fix: Errors show the real exit code, honor --no-color, and point at the config\r\n* db39c406 feat: `BasedOnStyles = NONE`, the spelled-out empty value\r\n* bc8b91d8 perf: Don't parse a file no rule can run on\r\n* c283a4dc feat: Conditional sections, `[glob if expr]`\r\n* 08923bdf feat: `vale test`, and install a package's own dependencies for it\r\n* 424f6e62 fix: Keep a fenced block skipped when both `pre` and `code` are in SkippedScopes\r\n* 84deb6c3 fix: Keep non-breaking and narrow spaces beside inline markup\r\n* 8cbda873 feat(code): parse C# comments with the C# grammar (#1196)\r\n* 24f277bb test: add `vale test` cases\r\n\r\n"
}
